{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-1qz:000001:issue_created:sase-1qz:9fe5ef0165432b20b6dd5658cd0f5e401fdb1c46f63ae5db99fd946d1b43bc3b","timestamp":"2026-11-02T22:42:13Z","actor":"bbugyi200.apollo.research.33.linker.w0","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-1qz","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-1qz","title":"Agent Hijack: stop a stalled agent, keep its work, recover in one keypress","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-11-02T22:42:13Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.apollo.research.33.linker.w0","updated_at":"2026-11-02T22:42:13Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"A user can hijack a stalled sase agent (,k, the kill dialog's h, or `sase agent hijack NAME`). Its process tree stops, but its workspace claim, Agents-tab node, and evidence stay. The node shows a ⏏ HIJACKED status, and <enter> opens a single-keypress recovery panel: escalate to a smarter model, continue, or instruct in the same workspace; restart or edit from a fresh workspace after a verified snapshot; view the diff, open a shell, or dismiss. Every path is durable, exactly-once, and fails closed so work is never silently lost.","design":"plan:202611/agent_hijack.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Approved epic plan plan:202611/agent_hijack.md requests this work","dependencies":[]}}}
